    "done_when": "A fenced launch whose declared write path lies in a directory that does not exist yet starts instead of failing in bwrap with \"Can't find source path\". Before the fence argv is built, the launch creates the missing directories of each declared write path under that path's own parent chain. It never binds an existing ancestor writable in place of the declared path, so the grant is no wider than declared. tests/test_fence_creates_a_missing_write_parent.py synthesises a run whose write path is tmp_path/reports/missing/report.md (tmp_path is the pytest fixture). It asserts that the composed argv's writable bind is exactly the declared directory or file, never tmp_path/reports. It asserts that the directory exists after composition. It also asserts that a launch whose write path cannot be created (its parent is a regular file) refuses with a message naming the path, rather than exiting 1 as an abandoned run. The negative control removes the directory creation, and the first assertion must fail with the missing-source condition. tests/test_each_run_owns_its_harness_home.py, tests/test_fence_is_on_again.py, tests/test_backend_environment.py and tests/test_a_fenced_worker_can_commit.py add no failures against the base. Gate and control logs go under the run directory, never in docs/figures. The change is committed in this worktree.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Create each declared write path's missing directories before a fenced launch binds them, so bwrap never aborts a run on a source path that does not exist yet.",
